# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, whatever the working tree
# uses. Without this, a file saved with CRLF on Windows reads as a whole-file
# rewrite in `git diff`, and a distracted `git add -A` commits that rewrite over
# every line the author never touched. Git detects binary content on its own and
# leaves it alone.
* text=auto

# The vendored Roblox document is copied byte for byte by .github/workflows/
# update-openapi.yml, and its diffs are read to spot real Roblox changes. Keep
# git out of its content entirely.
spec/openapi.json -text

# Rust sources check out with LF on every platform, not just in the repository.
# `text=auto` above normalises what is stored and then hands the working tree
# the platform's ending, so a Windows checkout gives `include_str!` and every
# multi-line string literal CRLF line endings. That is invisible until the
# literal is a shell script: `rbx completions bash` emits a hook that a shell
# refuses on line 1. Pinning the checkout ending is the fix that does not
# depend on remembering.
*.rs text eol=lf
